WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.900
Five drone strikes cut power for residents across three Sudanese states. This is Omni View Top World News, episode 34. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. After that blackout, Algeria's troop vote, a January football tournament set against Missile Fire, and maternity care in the Mississippi Delta. Sudan's rapid support forces hit two stations in Al Jazeera, two in Gadaraf and one in White Nile. A government official, unnamed, told the Guardian those three states are held by the Army, and that large

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.880
parts of them are now dark. The Army and the Rapid Support Forces, once allies, have been

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:39.700
fighting since April 2023. The United Nations has warned that strikes like these threaten

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:43.860
health care and other services for millions already in what it calls the world's largest

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:49.660
hunger crisis. In Al-Fau, in Gadarov, Babakir Yusuf said the lights went out early in the morning

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:55.160
and his diabetic son's insulin has to stay in a fridge. A United Nations tally counts more than

00:00:55.160 --> 00:01:00.000
300 people killed by drone strikes in the first three weeks of October, and hundreds more injured.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:05.500
Aid workers estimate the war has killed more than 200,000 people in a country of about 50 million.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:10.100
Most hospitals have been forced to shut, and at least 8 million children are out of school.

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:16.340
In Al-Janeid, Farmer Abdul-Hafaz-Dafala, 54, said a rec station had been repaired.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:20.500
Power had begun to improve three months ago, and then the station was hit again,

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.840
so his irrigation pumps still cannot run.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:28.720
Grocer Ebrahim Muhammad, 37, in Gadarov, said he may lose the chicken in his fridge or

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:29.700
dump it at any price.

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:33.380
The currency has lost more than a quarter of its value in recent weeks.

00:01:34.512 --> 00:01:37.732
Algeria's parliament on Sunday approved soldiers for neighboring Niger.

00:01:38.292 --> 00:01:43.572
The first time Algerian forces go abroad since they supported Egypt in the 1973 Arab-Israeli

00:01:43.572 --> 00:01:43.832
war.

00:01:44.392 --> 00:01:47.032
France 24 and Al-Jazeera both carried the vote.

00:01:47.452 --> 00:01:51.252
Every one of the 148 upper-house members in the room voted yes.

00:01:51.252 --> 00:01:56.592
A legislator told AFP, and the Lower House said it passed the plan by an absolute majority.

00:01:57.072 --> 00:01:58.752
The job is to guard energy sites.

00:01:59.132 --> 00:02:03.552
Senator Belkisem Bulghiti told the Associated Press the force would protect Algeria's

00:02:03.552 --> 00:02:06.832
interests, especially sonnetract oil facilities inside Niger.

00:02:07.352 --> 00:02:13.192
Armed groups keep hitting Niger, including near a desert border 960 kilometers long, and

00:02:13.192 --> 00:02:17.512
the two governments have agreed to work more closely against jihadist violence, cross-border

00:02:17.512 --> 00:02:18.392
crime and trafficking.

00:02:18.392 --> 00:02:23.652
Beijing. Niger's defense minister, Salifu Modi, was in Algiers on Wednesday, meeting

00:02:23.652 --> 00:02:28.972
President Abdul Majid Taboon and Army Chief Saeed Changriha. An Algerian report said a

00:02:28.972 --> 00:02:34.452
military cooperation protocol was signed. On October 3, Taboon said on television, we

00:02:34.452 --> 00:02:38.872
will protect Niger no matter what. And he said oil, mining, and other agreements were

00:02:38.872 --> 00:02:43.392
what others wanted to destroy. Nearly two months ago, Algeria sent four Russian-made

00:02:43.392 --> 00:02:49.632
Sukhoi SU-30 jets, plus a transport plane and a refueling aircraft to Niyamey, after authorities

00:02:49.632 --> 00:02:52.932
there described an attempt to destabilize the military-led government.

00:02:53.532 --> 00:02:56.432
Algiers had also given Niyamey four military helicopters.

00:02:56.832 --> 00:03:01.612
A 2020 constitutional change says troops may leave the country only with a two-thirds vote

00:03:01.612 --> 00:03:02.172
in parliament.

00:03:02.672 --> 00:03:08.812
The Stockholm International Peace Research Institute, cited by Al Jazeera, put Algiers 2025 military

00:03:08.812 --> 00:03:12.432
spending above $25 billion dollars, the largest in Africa.

00:03:12.432 --> 00:03:12.532
Russia.

00:03:13.012 --> 00:03:17.572
Researcher Abdelah Akir told AFP this breaks a doctrine of staying out of other people's

00:03:17.572 --> 00:03:22.072
wars, that it is meant to secure the Trans-Saharan gas pipeline from Nigeria through Niger

00:03:22.072 --> 00:03:26.892
toward Europe, and that it is a signal to Morocco and the United Arab Emirates, neither

00:03:26.892 --> 00:03:29.152
of which still has diplomatic ties with Algiers.

00:03:30.205 --> 00:03:35.805
Saudi Arabia will open the 2027 Asian Cup on January 7 in Riyadh against Palestine.

00:03:36.385 --> 00:03:39.705
Al-Jazeera reported the Asian Football Confederation's Monday schedule.

00:03:39.705 --> 00:03:46.145
The final is February 5th at King Fodd Sports City Stadium, 72,000 seats, which also stages

00:03:46.145 --> 00:03:46.645
the opener.

00:03:47.205 --> 00:03:53.125
51 matches in 29 days, 8 grounds, 5 in Riyadh, 2 in Jeddah, 1 in Al-Kobar.

00:03:53.585 --> 00:03:55.805
The local organizing committee is keeping those dates.

00:03:56.445 --> 00:04:01.945
AFC Chief Salman Bin Ibrahim Al-Khalifa said this month a delay to 2028 was possible if

00:04:01.945 --> 00:04:02.485
it had to be.

00:04:03.085 --> 00:04:07.885
Japan Football Association President Suni Yasumi Amodo said the news still made the country

00:04:07.885 --> 00:04:11.365
look unsafe, and that he did not think the cup would be easy to hold there.

00:04:11.785 --> 00:04:16.485
He also said Saudi officials told him the safety of players, fans, and everyone else coming

00:04:16.485 --> 00:04:17.645
was their first priority.

00:04:18.265 --> 00:04:23.405
Dakar rally organizers said Monday the 2027 race is leaving Saudi Arabia because of what

00:04:23.405 --> 00:04:24.625
has been happening in the region.

00:04:25.105 --> 00:04:28.565
On Sunday, the Saudi-led coalition intercepted a barrage from Yemen.

00:04:29.185 --> 00:04:34.205
Saudi civil defense said Shrapnel from two intercepted ballistic missiles, suspected to have been

00:04:34.205 --> 00:04:37.425
fired by Yemen's Houthis, came down in Jeddah, Taif,

00:04:37.785 --> 00:04:40.325
Rabiq, and Wadi al-Moghamas in Mecca province.

00:04:40.805 --> 00:04:43.445
Other big events have already been canceled or put off.

00:04:43.765 --> 00:04:46.445
International flights at King Khalid International Airport

00:04:46.445 --> 00:04:49.245
in Riyadh were due back from Terminal 2 on Sunday,

00:04:49.585 --> 00:04:51.365
with Terminal 1 for domestic flights,

00:04:51.805 --> 00:04:53.905
after suspensions that followed Houthi strikes,

00:04:54.265 --> 00:04:57.045
including one on October 10th, that killed 13 people

00:04:57.045 --> 00:04:58.125
and wounded hundreds.

00:04:58.605 --> 00:05:01.545
Several of the 24 federations have raised security worries.

00:05:01.545 --> 00:05:06.725
defending champion Qatar meets Thailand on January 11, the same day Japan plays

00:05:06.725 --> 00:05:11.305
Indonesia. This would be Saudi Arabia's first Asian Cup, seven years before it

00:05:11.305 --> 00:05:16.762
stages the 2034 World Cup. In the United States, a new March of Dimes report says

00:05:16.762 --> 00:05:20.702
nearly half of Mississippi's counties are maternity deserts. That means no

00:05:20.702 --> 00:05:25.502
obstetrician, no family doctor who delivers babies, no nurse midwife, no

00:05:25.502 --> 00:05:30.142
hospital, and no clinic, the Globe and Mail reported. Michael Warren, the group's

00:05:30.142 --> 00:05:34.402
chief medical and health officer called the gap the result of deliberate policy decisions

00:05:34.402 --> 00:05:36.162
and of how resources were allocated.

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:41.362
He said 17% of counties are one clinician away from having nobody left to give obstetric

00:05:41.362 --> 00:05:41.722
care.

00:05:42.282 --> 00:05:46.962
The Globe reports more infants die in Mississippi than in any other state and that too many mothers

00:05:46.962 --> 00:05:48.602
die of causes tied to pregnancy.

00:05:49.202 --> 00:05:53.762
Women travel long distances to deliver, which can mean skipped prenatal visits and a hard

00:05:53.762 --> 00:05:54.962
trip when labor starts.

00:05:54.962 --> 00:06:01.302
In Cleveland, Mississippi, Pam Chapman, 57, gives away baby supplies at boss lady for kids,

00:06:01.542 --> 00:06:05.742
with help from four good community, and she has brought fruit and vegetables to expectant

00:06:05.742 --> 00:06:10.022
mothers because obesity, diabetes, and high blood pressure are common risks there.

00:06:10.482 --> 00:06:15.422
She also runs free rides from the rural Delta to FedEx jobs in Memphis, and in the pandemic

00:06:15.422 --> 00:06:16.862
she helped get vaccines out.

00:06:17.262 --> 00:06:22.082
That Delta, the state's northwest corner along the Mississippi River, is known as the birthplace

00:06:22.082 --> 00:06:26.242
of the blues and of the civil rights movement, and neighbors are filling holes where services

00:06:26.242 --> 00:06:26.682
are thin.

00:06:27.809 --> 00:06:32.509
More than 730,000 Coloradans had already sent ballots back by Friday for the November

00:06:32.509 --> 00:06:33.289
3rd election.

00:06:33.909 --> 00:06:38.689
Colorado newsline, using Secretary of State figures, says that pace is set to rise well

00:06:38.689 --> 00:06:40.489
above the 2022 midterms.

00:06:40.849 --> 00:06:44.989
The paper frames the vote as a verdict on two years of Republican control in Washington

00:06:44.989 --> 00:06:48.389
under President Donald Trump and Republican majorities in Congress.

00:06:48.389 --> 00:06:52.849
It says tens of millions of dollars have gone into Colorado house races that will help

00:06:52.849 --> 00:06:54.169
decide who runs the chamber.

00:06:54.869 --> 00:06:58.709
Adams County officials covering the more Democratic-leaning half of the battleground

00:06:58.709 --> 00:07:02.869
eighth congressional district learned last week that Trump's Justice Department plans

00:07:02.869 --> 00:07:04.049
to send election monitors.

00:07:04.589 --> 00:07:06.929
Federal officials called that routine observation.

00:07:07.389 --> 00:07:10.109
State and local leaders have treated it as a cause for alarm.

00:07:10.609 --> 00:07:15.369
Newsline reported, the same account says Trump and his allies have pushed a mid-decade redraw

00:07:15.369 --> 00:07:20.649
districts and filed legal challenges in some states early amid growing fears the administration

00:07:20.649 --> 00:07:25.409
could interfere or refuse the result. Through election day and after, people can text

00:07:25.409 --> 00:07:31.469
newsline to a hotline the newsroom is watching, on eligibility, registration, the count and certification.

00:07:32.581 --> 00:07:38.601
In Serbia, Alexander Vucic said it is clear his party lost Sunday's snap election after 12 years in

00:07:38.601 --> 00:07:46.201
power. In Brazil, Luis Anasio Lula de Silva won a fourth term with 51.8% to Flavio Bolsonaro's

00:07:46.201 --> 00:07:51.861
48.2, the Globe and Mail reported, and Bolsonaro called for the election to be annulled. The

00:07:51.861 --> 00:07:57.121
New York Times reported. In the West Bank, Israel's offensive in Hebron has displaced more than

00:07:57.121 --> 00:08:04.361
2,600 Palestinians and Adola reported. In Caracas, opposition leader Maria Carina Machado came

00:08:04.361 --> 00:08:09.521
home after more than 10 months in exile, having left by speedboat, and thousands of supporters

00:08:09.521 --> 00:08:10.361
were there to meet her.

00:08:10.921 --> 00:08:15.601
In Uganda, the government has halved non-essential spending, and the central bank has warned

00:08:15.601 --> 00:08:16.281
of speculation.

